<h1 id="title">Woman</h1>
<p class="subtitle" id="subtitle">Some evidence is specific. Some context always applies.</p>
<p class="description" id="description">Evidence relevant to pregnancy, development, reproduction or a documented difference between sexes — when it exists, and when it does not.</p>
<div id="header_trigger_container"></div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<h2 class="section-title" id="why_title">Why this matters</h2>
<p class="section-intro" id="why_body">For decades, nutritional and toxicological research focused on the general population. Where evidence specific to women's biology exists, BOTIA shows it. Where it does not, BOTIA says so rather than assuming.</p>
</section>
<section class="section">
<h2 class="section-title" id="what_title">What BOTIA looks for</h2>
<p class="section-intro" id="what_body">BOTIA works in two ways here. When the label declares an ingredient with documented evidence relevant to pregnancy, development or reproduction, BOTIA flags it directly. When no such ingredient is found, BOTIA still surfaces context that does not depend on the ingredient list — such as packaging migrants or cumulative exposure — because that context exists regardless of what the label declares.</p>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="can-cannot">
<div class="can-box">
<h4 id="can_title">BOTIA CAN</h4>
<ul>
<li id="can_1">Detect declared ingredients backed by an official assessment relevant to pregnancy, development or reproductive health.</li>
<li id="can_2">Show context that does not appear on the ingredient list at all.</li>
<li id="can_3">Point to the specific assessment behind each finding.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="cannot-box">
<h4 id="cannot_title">BOTIA CANNOT</h4>
<ul>
<li id="cannot_1">Diagnose, assess personal risk, or replace medical advice.</li>
<li id="cannot_2">Detect contaminants or packaging migrants that the label does not declare.</li>
<li id="cannot_3">Tell you what to eat or avoid — that decision is always yours.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="closing">
<p class="closing-claim" id="closing">Evidence when it exists. Context when it does not. Never a verdict.</p>
